   "why": "A +3/+3 effect on the Ironsmith keeps applying after it transforms into Ironfang: 1/1 plus 3/3 is 4/4, and after the flip the base 3/1 plus the same 3/3 is 6/4. The runner starts the werewolf already flipped, so the setup first lets two spells be cast in turn 1 so the flip-back trigger returns it to the Ironsmith on the opponent's upkeep; only then is the pump cast, followed by Moonmist (which transforms Humans, and the Ironsmith is one). Without the flip the creature would stay 4/4.",
